.TH E621\-THUMBNAILER 1 "2026\-05\-13" "e621\-thumbnailer 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
e621\-thumbnailer \- generate image and animated thumbnails from e621 videos
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B e621\-thumbnailer
.I input
.RI [ options ]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B e621\-thumbnailer
downloads or reads a video file from e621 and extracts a thumbnail from a
randomly chosen point in the video.
.PP
.I input
may be any of:
.RS
.TP
.I post\-id
A numeric post ID (e.g.\& \fB4505261\fR).
The post is looked up via the e621 API and its file URL is used.
.TP
.I md5
A 32\-character hexadecimal MD5 hash.
The corresponding post is resolved through the e621 API.
.TP
.I url
A direct HTTP or HTTPS URL to a video file.
.TP
.I file
An absolute or relative path to a local video file.
.RE
.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Output
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIpath\fR
Write the thumbnail to
.IR path .
If omitted, the file is written to
.B thumbnail.\fIformat\fR
in the current directory.
Use
.B \-
to write the raw bytes to standard output instead;
status and progress messages are redirected to standard error in this mode.
.
.SS Type and format
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-type " " \fItype\fR
Thumbnail type.
.RS
.TP
.B image
Extract a single frame.
This is the default.
.TP
.B animated
Extract a short clip and encode it as an animated image.
.RE
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " " \fIfmt\fR
Output format.
For
.B image
thumbnails:
.BR png " (default), " jpg ", " webp .
For
.B animated
thumbnails:
.BR gif " (default), " webp .
.
.SS Image options
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-width " " \fIpx\fR
Scale the output to
.I px
pixels wide, preserving aspect ratio.
Set to
.B 0
to keep the original dimensions.
Default:
.BR 0 .
.TP
.BI \-\-jpeg\-quality " n"
JPEG encoding quality in the range
.BR 1 \(en 31 .
Lower values produce better quality and larger files.
Default:
.BR 2 .
Only used when
.B \-\-format jpg
is set.
.TP
.BI \-\-webp\-quality " n"
WebP encoding quality in the range
.BR 0 \(en 100 .
Default:
.BR 85 .
Only used when
.B \-\-format webp
is set.
.
.SS Animated options
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-width " " \fIpx\fR
Scale the output to
.I px
pixels wide.
Default:
.BR 480 .
.TP
.BI \-\-length " seconds"
Duration of the extracted clip in seconds.
Longer clips increase both processing time and file size significantly.
Default:
.BR 2.5 .
.TP
.BI \-\-fps " n"
Frames per second of the output.
Reducing this is one of the most effective ways to shrink GIF file size.
Default:
.BR 15 .
.TP
.BI \-\-colors " n"
Number of colours in the GIF palette.
Must be between
.B 2
and
.BR 256 .
Fewer colours produce smaller files at the cost of quality.
Default:
.BR 128 .
Only used when
.B \-\-format gif
is set.
.TP
.BI \-\-quality " n"
WebP encoding quality in the range
.BR 0 \(en 100 .
Default:
.BR 75 .
Only used when
.B \-\-format webp
is set.
.TP
.BI \-\-gif\-optimize " level"
Optimisation level passed to
.BR gifsicle (1)
after encoding, in the range
.BR 0 \(en 3 .
.B 0
disables optimisation entirely.
Levels
.BR 1 \(en 3
correspond to gifsicle's
.BR \-O1 ", " \-O2 ", " \-O3
flags respectively.
Requires
.B gifsicle
to be present in
.BR PATH .
Default:
.BR 0 .
Only used when
.B \-\-format gif
is set.
.
.SS Binary paths
.TP
.BI \-\-ffmpeg " path"
Absolute path to the
.B ffmpeg
binary.
If omitted, the path bundled with the
.B ffmpeg\-static
package is used when available, otherwise
.B ffmpeg
is looked up in
.BR PATH .
.TP
.BI \-\-ffprobe " path"
Absolute path to the
.B ffprobe
binary.
If omitted, the path bundled with the
.B ffprobe\-static
package is used when available, otherwise
.B ffprobe
is looked up in
.BR PATH .
.
.SS Miscellaneous
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit with status
.BR 0 .
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Thumbnail generated and saved successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments, or an error occurred during generation.
.
.SH EXAMPLES
Generate a PNG thumbnail for post 4505261 and save it to the current directory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
e621\-thumbnailer 4505261
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generate a 3\-second animated GIF with gifsicle level\-2 optimisation:
.PP
.RS
.nf
e621\-thumbnailer 4505261 \-t animated \-\-length 3 \-\-gif\-optimize 2 \-o out.gif
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generate an animated WebP from an MD5 hash:
.PP
.RS
.nf
e621\-thumbnailer a51d55b12e7a16a37253783e52c4ec21 \-t animated \-f webp \-o out.webp
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generate a JPEG thumbnail from a local file at a specific width:
.PP
.RS
.nf
e621\-thumbnailer ./video.webm \-f jpg \-w 640 \-o thumb.jpg
.fi
.RE
.PP
Pipe a PNG thumbnail directly into
.BR display (1)
without writing a file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
e621\-thumbnailer 4505261 \-o \- | display
.fi
.RE
.PP
Pipe an animated GIF into a network socket:
.PP
.RS
.nf
e621\-thumbnailer 4505261 \-t animated \-o \- | nc host 1234
.fi
.RE
.PP
Specify explicit binary paths when neither system binaries nor the static
packages are available:
.PP
.RS
.nf
e621\-thumbnailer 4505261 \-\-ffmpeg /opt/ffmpeg/bin/ffmpeg \e
    \-\-ffprobe /opt/ffmpeg/bin/ffprobe
.fi
.RE
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR ffprobe (1),
.BR gifsicle (1)
.
